{
  "_comment": [
    "Retailer-order scenarios for the shared pricing module (issue #8).",
    "Every expected amount is hand-calculated in integer SGD cents.",
    "alpha's free-delivery threshold is 5999 so the boundary can be probed at",
    "5998, 5999 and 6000 using whole packs of real-looking prices.",
    "Retailer rules here are invented for testing; the verified Singapore",
    "delivery scenarios belong to curation (issue #4, PR-04).",
    "Orders assembled wrongly by a caller (no lines, or a line from another",
    "retailer) throw rather than returning a status, and are tested in",
    "order.test.ts instead.",
    "The keys under \"retailers\" (alpha, beta, ...) name test rule sets, not retailers.",
    "Each rule set carries one of the contract's real retailer IDs, and its offers share it;",
    "several rule sets may use the same ID because no scenario mixes them.",
    "zeta has an unresolved fee but a free-delivery threshold, to show that reaching",
    "the threshold prices the order while falling short still blocks it."
  ],
  "retailers": {
    "alpha": {
      "retailerId": "redmart",
      "verified": true,
      "fee": 599,
      "freeDeliveryThreshold": 5999,
      "minimumOrder": 2000,
      "thresholdBasis": {
        "includesMandatoryCharges": false
      },
      "orderCharges": []
    },
    "beta": {
      "retailerId": "fairprice",
      "verified": true,
      "fee": 350,
      "freeDeliveryThreshold": null,
      "minimumOrder": null,
      "thresholdBasis": {
